Filter is component that sits between servlet API and the dispatcher servlet which is used to intercept the request from client
and response from controllers and modify the requests and response. These filters are mainly used for applying the cross
cutting concerns like security, logging etc to the incoming http requests.

Filter chain is the group of filters chained so that our http request will be going through all of the filter logics and
then passed to the dispatcher servlet.

We can implement custom filter by implementing the Filter interface and its doFilter method which accepts ServletRequest, ServletResponse
and Filter chain.

doFilter(ServletRequest servletRequest, ServletResponse response, FilterChain chain){
HttpServletRequest request=(HttpServlet)servletRequest;
request.getRemoteAdress();
}

servletRequest.doFilter(servletRequest, servletResponse);

Use cases of Filter in real time:
1. Validating the JWT token.
2. Performing the logging.
3. Tracking the client based on the IP. Logging the headers and 
4. Modifying the HTTP headers(Injecting correlation-Id)
5. Rate Limiting: Limiting the exxesive traffic from a specific client with the IP
6. Request Validation like validating content-type, request size.

